# C#/.NET testing

Narrows `core-common-rules`' stack-agnostic testing rules to xUnit/NUnit
convention and disciplined mocking with Moq/NSubstitute. Applies only to
`*.cs` files.

## Framework and layout

- Match the project's test framework (xUnit or NUnit); do not add a second.
  xUnit: `[Fact]`, `[Theory]` + `[InlineData(...)]`/`[MemberData(...)]`.
  NUnit: `[Test]`, `[TestCase(...)]`.
- Tests live in a mirrored `*.Tests`/`*.Test` project (`Orders/` and
  `Orders.Tests/`), not inside the production project.
- Name a test `MethodName_Scenario_ExpectedResult`
  (`Validate_MissingOrderId_ThrowsArgumentException`).

## Table-driven (`Theory`/`TestCase`) tests

- `[Theory]` + `[InlineData(...)]` (xUnit) or `[TestCase(...)]` (NUnit) for
  cases on the same method, not a copy-pasted `[Fact]`/`[Test]` per case.
- `[MemberData(nameof(Cases))]`/`TestCaseSource` for non-primitive case
  values.

## Async tests

- A test of `async` code is `async Task` and awaits the call under test;
  never `async void`, never a blocking `.Result`/`.Wait()`.

## Mocking boundaries: mock the seam, not the internals

- Mock/stub an external dependency the unit talks to through an interface
  (an `HttpClient`-backed client, a repository interface, a clock, a message
  publisher) with Moq (`Mock<IThing>`) or NSubstitute
  (`Substitute.For<IThing>()`).
- Do not mock an internal collaborator that is part of what the test
  verifies (a private helper, a concrete value object, the class's own logic
  split into another method).
- Before adding a mock, check whether the real system crosses a
  process/network/disk boundary there (HTTP, database, filesystem, clock,
  random); only that earns a mock, not a class your own code owns.
- Verify a mock's interaction (`mock.Verify(...)`/`receivedCall.Received()`)
  only for a call that is itself part of the contract ("an email is sent
  exactly once"), not incidental implementation detail.

## Assertions and determinism

- The project's adopted assertion style (xUnit `Assert`, or FluentAssertions
  if already a dependency); do not add a second library.
- Never `Thread.Sleep`/`Task.Delay` to wait for async work; await the
  `Task`, or use `TaskCompletionSource` or a cancellation-bounded wait.
- Reset/dispose a shared fixture (`IClassFixture<T>`,
  `WebApplicationFactory<TEntryPoint>`) between cases that mutate shared
  state.
